# An argument of the wrong type points at the argument and lists the signature.
mode: check
schema: 'orders.csv'(orderId: string, customerId: string, amount: real, qty: long, small: int, timestamp: datetime, wait: timespan, shipped: bool)
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where strlen(qty) > 1;
from 'orders.csv' | where iff(shipped, 1, customerId) > 1
---- expected
error[DS2006]: argument `source` of `strlen` must be `string`, found `long`
  --> query:1:34
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where strlen(qty) > 1;
  |                                  ^^^ this is `long` (column `qty` was read from orders.csv)
  |
  = help: convert it first if that is what you meant: `tostring(qty)`
  = note: signature: `strlen(source: string) -> long`

error[DS2006]: argument `else` of `iff` must have the same type as argument `then` (`long`), found `string`
  --> query:2:43
  |
2 | from 'orders.csv' | where iff(shipped, 1, customerId) > 1
  |                                        -  ^^^^^^^^^^ this is `string` (column `customerId` was read from orders.csv)
  |                                        |
  |                                        this is `long`
  |
  = help: convert it first if that is what you meant: `tolong(customerId)`
  = note: signature: `iff(condition: bool, then: T, else: T) -> T`
